    "reply": "The retrieved records are BRCA1 missense variants named on the NM_007294.4 transcript, but they contain no clinical-significance calls, review evidence, or genome-assembly coordinates, so they only partly answer the question. One representative variant is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4709T>C (p.Leu1570Pro) [1].\n\n## Variant Identifiers\n\nThe variants are named in standard HGVS form against NM_007294.4 and carry ClinVar identifiers. ClinVar:1000183 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4709T>C (p.Leu1570Pro) [1]. ClinVar:1001081 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.353T>C (p.Leu118Pro) [3]. ClinVar:1010734 is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4840C>G (p.Pro1614Ala) [30]. One record, ClinVar:1010631, has an identifier but no variant name [29].\n\n## Distribution Along the Protein\n\nThe substitutions span the coding sequence, from the N-terminal region to the C-terminal region. Near the N-terminus is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.353T>C (p.Leu118Pro) [3]. In the central region is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.3664G>A (p.Glu1222Lys) [2]. Toward the C-terminus is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4685C>G (p.Pro1562Arg) [12].\n\n## Evidence Gaps\n\nThe records give no pathogenicity classification, submitter evidence, or GRCh37/GRCh38 placement. To get that detail, retrieve each ClinVar record live.",
